    "summary": "Root cause: the accepted decision lane.xi had a wrong (stale) value of 0.78. The bridge has 2 design lanes (two-way traffic, 9 m carriageway), so JTG D60-2015 Table 4.3.1-5 gives the transverse lane-load factor xi = 1.0 (0.78 is the value for 3 lanes). L2-1 re-computes each member parameter via the rule/code formulas from the instance trail, so the mismatch between the model parameter (0.78) and the clause formula result (1.0) made L2-1 fail. I corrected lane.xi to 1.0 (evidence JTGD60-4.3.1-xi, INPUT:deck.design_lanes, dec:lane.n_lanes); no instance data was wrong, so write_instance was not needed. Regeneration then passed all L1/L2/L3 checks.\n\nFinal model (spine-beam 2D, simply supported, single 30 m span):\n- Girder: 3 precast prestressed small-box girders (C40); single-girder A = 1.13893 m^2, I = 0.35492 m^4; combined A = 3.41679 m^2, I = 1.06475 m^4; Ec = 32500 MPa, gamma = 26 kN/m^3; w = 88.836 kN/m, m = 9.0557 t/m (consistent mass).\n- Supports (2 abutments): plain laminated elastomeric bearings, 6 per line (2 per girder end x 3 girders), 300x400 mm, 5x8 mm rubber; S = 10.714, Kv = 8.518e6 kN/m, Kh = 18000 kN/m per line; vertical/longitudinal springs, rotation free.\n- Live load (HL Class II): 2 design lanes, xi = 1.0, qk = 7.875 kN/m, Pk = 240 kN, mu = 0.2006 (from f1).\n- Results: f1 = 3.402 Hz; total self-weight reaction = 1332.55 kN per abutment; self-weight midspan moment = 9994.1 kNm; lane-load max positive moment = 6449.6 kNm."
